5B. Digit DP - Counting Numbers with a Digit-Based
Condition
CO5 | BTL-4
Description
Digit DP counts numbers in a range [L, R] that satisfy a condition on their digits (e.g. digit sum equals S, no digit 4,
no repeated digit) without checking every number. The number is built digit by digit from left to right. The state is
(position, extra info, tight), where the extra info is what the condition needs (here: the digit sum so
far), and tight says whether the digits chosen so far equal the prefix of the limit N. If tight, the next digit is at most
N's digit; otherwise any digit 0-9 is allowed. States are memoised because many prefixes lead to the same state.
For a range, the answer is count(R) - count(L-1).
Algorithm
1. Convert the limit N into a list of digits.
2. Define go(i, s, tight): number of ways to fill digits i..end given sum s so far.
3. Base case: if all digits are placed, return 1 if s == S, else 0 (prune if s > S).
4. Try each allowed digit x (up to N's digit if tight); recurse with s + x and tight and x == limit.
5. Memoise and return go(0, 0, True).
